# TDPQA → QA Test (mandatory fields)

Moving a **TDPQA** bug to **QA Test** fails unless these ticket fields are filled
(workflow popup). Do **not** put the only handoff in a comment anymore.

| Display name | Field key | Notes |
|--------------|-----------|-------|
| RCA | `customfield_11999` | 3 short plain sentences: what happened / why / what we changed |
| Impact Analysis Details | `customfield_12008` | 3 bullets: fixed / unchanged / how QA should retest |
| Pre /Post Deployment Scripts | `customfield_12007` | `NA` / `NA` when no script |
| AiTDP Dev Improvement Remarks | `customfield_12000` | How AI helped (analysis → fix → check) — no Cursor brand |
| AiTDP Dev Accuracy | `customfield_12001` | **Whole percent** (e.g. `80`), not `0.80` |
| AiTDP Fix Quality Grade | `customfield_12002` | Short text `A`/`B`/`NA` — **mandatory for QA Test** |
| AiTDP Fix Quality Score | `customfield_12003` | Number (often same as Dev Accuracy) — **mandatory for QA Test** |
| AiTDP Lead Accuracy | `customfield_12004` | **Whole percent** 0–100 — mandatory for transition (popup) |
| AiTDP Lead Improvement Remarks | `customfield_12005` | Lead view of AI help — mandatory for transition |
| JIRA As per AI TDP Temp | `customfield_12009` | Yes `12785` when AI assisted |
| Micro Service | `customfield_12006` | Accounting `12770` (etc.) |
| Dev / QA Owner | `11952` / `11953` | via `owners_tdpqa` |
| **Dev Test Details** | *(no field)* | **Required in pack as `dev[]`** → companion comment headed **Dev Test Details** |

## Language (hard)

- Simple business words a QA person can read in 30 seconds.
- No branch, SHA, class/processor names, harness, ntest, SQL dumps.
- No `@darpan`. No other ticket keys unless the user asked.
- Prefer "delayed payment interest" over DPIC jargon when the ticket uses plain words; match the ticket's own wording when QA already used a term.

## Push before enrich (mandatory)

Before filling fields / moving to **QA Test**: prove the fix is on **`origin/<reported-train>`** (e.g. `origin/mfi_integration_v3.5.2.2`), not only `origin/fix/…`. Feature-branch-only ≠ QA-ready. Skill: `jira-fix-update` § Push gate.

## Agent path (mandatory)

```bash
# 0) Push gate — origin/<train> tip includes the fix (fetch + log/show)
python3 scripts/bin/jira-fix-adf.py project_mode TDPQA-NNN
# → mode=tdpqa_field_handoff

bash scripts/bin/jira-enrich.sh pack TDPQA-NNN payload.json > /tmp/pack.json
bash scripts/bin/jira-enrich.sh post TDPQA-NNN payload.json
```

Payload shape (same helper as SDCP, TDPQA field IDs):

```json
{
  "rca": { "situation": "…", "cause": "…", "resolution": "…" },
  "impact": ["Fixes …", "Does not change …", "Please retest …"],
  "pre": "NA",
  "post": "NA",
  "micro": ["accounting"],
  "aitdp_percent": 0.80,
  "aitdp_remarks": "Helped review the QA case, found …, fixed …, checked … before sending to QA.",
  "dev": [
    "Functional step QA can follow. Result: Pass."
  ],
  "qa_retest": [
    "After the accounting build is shared, retest on the reported loan."
  ],
  "ping_comment": "@Srikant @Reema Fix is ready for QA. Dev Test Details below."
}
```

Fields unblock **QA Test**. Pack **fails closed** without `dev[]` (no Dev Test field on TDPQA — companion comment is the product for retest steps). Existing long handoff comments may stay; do not invent a companion SDCP ticket.

## Status

After fields are non-null, transition toward **QA Test** when the workflow allows.
Never use **QA:Traige** as a substitute for QA Retest. If the needed transition is missing, report available transitions and leave status as-is.

